# Skill: Integration Routing

Purpose:
  Engineering skill for wiring external integrations (tools, channels,
  MCP servers, providers) with ordered backend routing, real health
  probing, and credential boundaries. Use when adding or operating any
  external capability.

Owns: engineering/integration-routing.sdd

Source: https://github.com/Panniantong/Agent-Reach (MIT — LICENSE,
  pyproject.toml; analyzed 2026-09-10; patterns from channels/base.py,
  doctor.py, probe.py, skill/SKILL_en.md)

Patterns:
  ordered_backends:
    - per-channel ordered candidate list; backends[0] preferred, rest
      fallbacks; switching = REORDER, never rewrite ([IR-01..03])
  user_override_safety:
    - `<channel>_backend` override moves a backend to front; UNKNOWN
      override values are IGNORED — stale overrides never hide working
      backends
  real_probing:
    - 4-way probe classification: missing / broken (stale venv shim,
      exit 126/127, FileNotFoundError → reinstall prescription) /
      timeout / error; existence is NOT health ([IR-02])
    - probes side-effect-free; retries only transient statuses ([IR-05])
  doctor_discipline:
    - per-channel self-check; one failing channel degrades to its own
      row, never crashes the report ([IR-06])
    - tier-grouped report: 0 zero-config / 1 free-key / 2 setup
    - stale active_backend must not leak from a previous check
  credential_boundaries:
    - local-only storage (600 perms); no agent-login-for-user; no
      browser-cookie reads; env-only injection, values never logged;
      dedicated low-value accounts for ban-risk platforms ([SEC-09..13])
  output_scrubbing:
    - URL credentials scrubbed at output boundary — upstream output can
      echo configured URLs ([SEC-12])
  capability_layer_philosophy:
    - the layer SELECTS, installs, health-checks, routes; reading is
      done by the agent calling upstream tools directly — no wrapper
      ([IR-10]; matches SDDRA spec-first no-bloat philosophy)
  backend_provenance:
    - announce "using X via Y" before use; record serving backend in
      outputs ([RS1-11])

AntiPatterns:
  - wrapper layers around upstream tools (capability layer ≠ proxy)
  - which()-style existence checks reported as health
  - blanket retries on missing/broken probes
  - credentials in logs or rendered health output
  - agent automating user login or reading cookie stores

Rules:
  [INTG1] Apply via .sdd/runtime/integration-routing.sdd — spec is authority.
  [INTG2] Integration designs cite their pattern provenance.

